# HIVMeet Frontend - AI Agent Rules (Cursor)

**Version**: 3.0 (Skills Centralized)
**Date**: 2026-04-12
**Project**: HIVMeet - Dating App for People Living with HIV/AIDS
**Stack**: Flutter (Dart) + Django (Python) + Firebase

## Startup (MANDATORY - execute BEFORE every request)

1. Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) first for routing rules
2. Read [.agents/skills/task-router/SKILL.md](.agents/skills/task-router/SKILL.md) and apply its decision tree to identify relevant skills
3. Load only the skill(s) returned by task-router
4. Follow the loaded skill workflow completely before responding

## Critical Rules

### 1. Backend API Contract Compliance
- Always consult API_DOCUMENTATION.md before any endpoint work
- Never guess endpoints or payloads

### 2. Mandatory Internationalization (FR/EN)
- Zero hardcoded strings allowed
- Use intl/ARB for all user-facing text

### 3. Centralized API Configuration
- Use ONLY lib/core/config/constants.dart for base URLs
- Never hardcode URLs

### 4. Privacy & Security
- Use flutter_secure_storage for tokens
- Never log PII (email, token, user ID, phone, location)

### 5. Non-Regression
- Always verify primary feature behavior after changes
- Test related flows impacted by the change

### 6. HIVMeet Domain Sensitivity
- All content must be respectful, non-stigmatizing, inclusive
- Respect user privacy settings

### 7. Complete Response Requirements
For every task:
1. Exact file paths to modify
2. Complete functional code (no pseudocode)
3. Specification compliance check
4. Non-regression validation
5. Backend impact (if applicable)
6. Concise summary

